FINAL ANSWER:
**Recommended reviewer: Troy Goode.** They hold the most surviving lines in `lib/index.js` and are the only active owner.

| Author | Surviving lines | Share | Commits | Last commit | Activity |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode <<email redacted>> | 132 | 61.7% | 28 | 2016-08-23 | inactive |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 20 | 9.3% | 4 | 2017-10-04 | inactive |
| Alejandro Caravaca Puchades | 14 | 6.5% | 5 | 2015-05-28 | inactive |
| Troy Goode <troy@laptop.example> | 12 | 5.6% | 1 | 2026-04-10 | active |
| LuisEGR | 6 | 2.8% | 1 | 2021-07-20 | inactive |

- **Troy Goode, merged:** 144 lines (67.3%), across two addresses. The output treats this as a strong identity match, so lead with the merged figure and keep the unmerged figures next to it. It rests on matching names and addresses, not on a `.mailmap` entry, so only you can confirm it is one person.
- **Next in line:** Douglas Christopher Wilson (9.3%) and Alejandro Caravaca Puchades (6.5%). Both are inactive by the tool's reference date. Alejandro also appears as "alex94puchades" with the same address, adding 1 commit and 14 lines.
- **Other 20 authors:** the output does not list them. Together they hold the remaining lines.
- **Bus factor:** 1. Troy Goode alone holds 61.7% of the 214 non-blank lines (61.8% of 238 with blank lines). Four authors are needed to reach 80%. Bus factor here means how concentrated the surviving code is, not who understands it.
- **Scope and method:** the figures cover this file only, at HEAD, using `git blame -w -M -C`. Blame takes the same ownership view whether or not you pass `--merge-identities`.
- **Not yet checked:** commit `fcd2b56` ("issue #42: (WIP) switch to ESLint; clean up", Troy Goode, 6 surviving lines) looks mechanical but was not set aside. Inspect it with `git show --stat fcd2b56` before relying on the 6-line figure.

Before you change the file, ask Troy Goode to review. If they are unavailable, Douglas Christopher Wilson or Alejandro Caravaca Puchades are the next candidates, but both have not committed for years. The activity markers use 2026-04-12 as the reference date, not today (2026-10-23).

